sers/arpang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-04T20:12:35Z","updated_at":"2024-11-07T05:01:49Z","closed_at":"2024-11-07T05:01:49Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-13864](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-13864)\r\n### Description\n\nCommit cceafbba926085b678c5cf7f2b5b94e0a81f1f8f modified pg_node_tree_in to support ysql_upgrade. \r\n\r\nThe pg15 merge changed the pg_node_tree handler to use a default function:\r\n```\r\nPSEUDOTYPE_DUMMY_INPUT_FUNC(pg_node_tree);\r\n\r\n/*\r\n * These macros generate input and output functions for a pseudo-type that\r\n * will reject all input and output attempts.  (But for some types, only\r\n * the input function need be dummy.)\r\n */\r\n#define PSEUDOTYPE_DUMMY_INPUT_FUNC(typname) \\\r\nDatum \\\r\ntypname##_in(PG_FUNCTION_ARGS) \\\r\n{ \\\r\n\tereport(ERROR, \\\r\n\t\t\t(errcode(ERRCODE_FEATURE_NOT_SUPPORTED), \\\r\n\t\t\t errmsg(\"cannot accept a value of type %s\", #typname))); \\\r\n\\\r\n\tPG_RETURN_VOID();\t\t\t/* keep compiler quiet */ \\\r\n} \\\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo the special handling added by the ysql_upgrade diff is missing. \r\n\r\nTest case:\r\n```\r\nSET ysql_upgrade_mode = true;\r\nSET yb_non_ddl_txn_for_sys_tables_allowed TO true;\r\nUPDATE pg_catalog.pg_proc SET\r\n  pronargs = 1,\r\n  pronargdefaults = 1,\r\n  proargtypes = '16',\r\n  proargnames = '{check_legacy}',\r\n  proargdefaults = '({CONST :consttype 16 :consttypmod -1 :constcollid 0 :constlen 1 :constbyval true :constisnull false :location 83 :constvalue 1 [ 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 ]})'\r\nWHERE proname = 'yb_is_database_colocated' AND proargtypes = '' AND pronamespace = 'pg_catalog'::regnamespace;\r\n```\r\n\r\nErrors with `ERROR:  can